<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41119" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕnŏvātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen., <i>a renewing</i>, <i>renewal</i>
			(Ciceron.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mundi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 46, 118</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">doctrinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Brut. 71, 250</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">timoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 11, 18, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Tit. 3, 5</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> In partic., in
			business lang., <i>a renewing of interest</i>, <i>compound interest</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">confeceram, ut solverent, centesimis sexennii
					ductis cum renovatione singulorum annorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 6, 1, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">auspiciorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					5, 52, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
